    {
      "command": "employee assign_skill 2 skill:driving.drill_rig level:1",
      "description": "Left unmarked: hiring already grants blasting at Rookie (ROLE_STARTING_QUALIFICATION), but no role starts with driving.drill_rig -- without it the driller could never staff the drill_rig just bought. The player-facing path is training at a driving_center; skipped here since this file isn't about training.",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "employee assign_skill 2 skill:driving.drill_rig level:1"
        }
      ],
      "role": "bootstrap"
    },
    {
      "command": "drill_plan grid rows:3 cols:3 spacing:2 depth:6 start:20,20",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"blast\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"grid-tool\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-param-strip [data-field=\"spacing\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "dragTiles",
          "x1": 20,
          "z1": 20,
          "x2": 24,
          "z2": 24
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "orderedHoleCount": 9,
          "holeCount": 0
        }
      },
      "description": "depth corrected from 8 to 6 (Ground rule #15/Finding #42's class, the whole-suite audit before Phase 3): this step never clicks the grid tool's depth stepper (data-field=\"depth\"), so the real drag always produces the panel's own 6m default regardless of what's declared. This file's own expect blocks only assert hole/charge/sequence counts around the affected blast (depth-insensitive), so this is a metadata-only correction -- verified both modes still pass unchanged. #553: spacing tightened from 5m to 2m to keep this 9-hole grid's drilling time reasonable for a single driller/drill_rig (no staffed:true near-origin spawn on a campaign map)."
    },
    {
      "command": "tick 50",
      "description": "#553: drain the ordered plan in bounded 50-tick chunks -- each chunk is followed by `event choose 0` since a `tick` command stops dead the instant a timer event fires mid-block (events.ts).",
      "interaction": [{"type": "command", "command": "tick 50"}],
      "role": "setup"
    },
    {
      "command": "event choose 0",
      "interaction": [{"type": "resolveEventIfPending"}],
      "role": "player"
